### IntelliJ HTTP Client file - open in IntelliJ IDEA (Ultimate or Community 2023.2+) and press the green arrows.
### Start the app first (see README). Run requests top to bottom; tokens and ids are stored automatically.

### 1) Register a business (tenant) + its ADMIN user
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "businessName": "Sharma Kirana Store",
  "adminName": "Ravi Sharma",
  "email": "ravi@sharma-kirana.test",
  "password": "Passw0rd!123"
}

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 2) (Optional) Login again later
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ravi@sharma-kirana.test", "password": "Passw0rd!123" }

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 3) Create a STAFF user (ADMIN only)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Meena Staff",
  "email": "meena@sharma-kirana.test",
  "password": "Passw0rd!123",
  "role": "STAFF"
}

### 4) Create a warehouse
POST http://localhost:8080/api/warehouses
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Main Godown", "location": "Pune" }

> {% client.global.set("warehouseId", response.body.id); %}

### 5) Create a product
POST http://localhost:8080/api/products
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "RICE-5KG",
  "name": "Basmati Rice 5kg",
  "description": "Premium aged basmati",
  "price": 499.00,
  "lowStockThreshold": 5
}

> {% client.global.set("productId", response.body.id); %}

### 6) Receive stock (positive delta). Negative delta = write-off.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/stock/adjust
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": {{productId}}, "warehouseId": {{warehouseId}}, "delta": 20, "note": "Initial purchase" }

### 7) Read product twice - second call is served from Redis
GET http://localhost:8080/api/products/{{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 8) Search products
GET http://localhost:8080/api/products?q=rice&page=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 9) Place an order -> 202 PENDING, processed asynchronously through RabbitMQ
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "Asha Verma",
  "customerEmail": "asha@example.test",
  "warehouseId": {{warehouseId}},
  "items": [ { "productId": {{productId}}, "quantity": 3 } ]
}

> {% client.global.set("orderId", response.body.id); %}

### 10) Check the order (CONFIRMED or REJECTED after a moment)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 11) Stock levels
GET http://localhost:8080/api/stock?productId={{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 12) Audit trail of stock movements
GET http://localhost:8080/api/stock/audit?productId={{productId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 13) Stock that is currently low
GET http://localhost:8080/api/stock/low
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 14) Alerts raised by the scheduled scan (every 5 minutes by default)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/alerts
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 15) Cancel an order (confirmed orders return their stock)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 16) Health
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health
